{"kind":"request","text":"E1 after-view source audit found one capability-record boundary before client projection wiring. It is not an operation-ID problem: ordinary operation effects require Native givenTo and already stop under ef1; current written operation opens are timed-only.\n\nActual case: device-command.open builds a command record with key:[given.self] and values.targetAt:given.self (derive/src/capability/device-command.ts:44-46, deriveEffect:128). These positions are not emitted written from:self ref effects, so the approved selfRefs index metadata does not identify them. The open command count feeds whole-scope reservations (same file:109-114). An after-view that simply delegates records/reservations to the recorded state would misjudge later acts.\n\nProposed bounded implementation: retain these record effects in a private overlay with a per-source alias, project actual recordCount/reservation changes, and represent their commit-dependent positions with the existing {entry:Source} family wherever exposed. Use explicit provenance from the capability effect, never numeric equality with a guessed sequence. This adds positions that the current from:self callback does not cover; please authorize that extension or choose a narrower result.\n\nAlternative: an act reaching this capability effect is unavailable until recorded. That would be broader than the missing-intent rule and must be an explicit decision, with affected acts listed. No new symbolic family, speculative Entry/hash, operation scope or second evaluator is proposed. Both source lanes hold this projection portion; independent types, basis binding and templates proceed.","body":{"conditions":"Choose the bounded hypothetical representation for device-command records whose self positions are not written from:self refs. Do not silently broaden unavailability or invent commit positions.","no_git_artifact":"true","stale_bases":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:ef1fc9326280ae6b